    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147-a9">

                <pb facs="0242" n="134" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg134"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8 in No.
                    173–—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister for Foreign Affairs to the Diplomatic
                        Corps.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-01-25"><hi rendition="#italic">January 25,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The minister of foreign affairs communicates to the representatives of England,
                    Italy, the United States of America, France, and Portugal that the insurgents,
                    profiting by the action of the vice-president of the republic, inspired by their
                    note of the 14th instant, in having the guns withdrawn from the battery on Bom
                    Jesus Island, occupied this latter at 4 o’clock on the morning of the 24th.</p>
            </div>
